---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Refund, Cancellation & Fulfillment Policies — Coopers Grass Fed Beef"
  description="Our refund, cancellation, shipping and fulfillment policies for every Coopers Grass Fed Beef share order. Effective November 15, 2026."
>
  <section class="bg-cream">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-5 md:px-8 py-16 md:py-24">
      <nav class="text-[13px] text-ink/50 mb-6">
        <a href="/" class="hover:text-pasture transition">Home</a>
        <span class="mx-2">/</span>
        <span>Policies</span>
      </nav>

      <div class="text-[12px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-gold mb-3">Our Policies</div>
      <h1 class="font-display text-[clamp(2rem,4.5vw,3rem)] tracking-tight text-ink leading-[1.1]">
        Refund, Cancellation &amp; Fulfillment Policies
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[15px] text-ink/60">
        Effective November 15, 2026 &middot; Applies to all beef and pork share orders.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-8 bg-white border border-black/10 rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-8 text-[15px] text-ink/80 leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          Every Coopers share is a <strong>custom order</strong>: we reserve a specific
          animal for you, schedule it for processing, and cut and wrap it to
          your cut sheet. Because the meat is made to order and perishable, our
          policies below are built around that process.
          <strong>Placing a deposit means you have read and agree to these terms.</strong>
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-[14px] text-ink/60">
          <strong>Time zone:</strong> All deadlines, business hours, and durations
          in this policy are measured in <strong>Central Time (CT)</strong> — our local
          time in Amarillo, TX. "Business days" means Monday–Friday, excluding
          U.S. federal holidays.
        </p>
      </div>

      <section class="mt-12">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-ink mb-4">1. Deposits &amp; Payment</h2>
        <p class="text-[15px] text-ink/70 mb-4">
          <strong>A $500 deposit reserves your animal and locks in your price.</strong>
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-[15px] text-ink/80 leading-relaxed marker:text-pasture">
          <li>
            A <strong>$500 deposit</strong> is required to reserve your share and lock in
            your price. Your order is not confirmed until the deposit is received.
          </li>
          <li>
            The <strong>remaining balance is due before your order ships</strong> or is
            released for local pickup. We'll send you the balance amount when
            your order is ready.
          </li>
          <li>
            Accepted payment methods: <strong>Zelle, Cash App, Apple Pay, Cash</strong>,
            and card payments through the secure payment link on our website.
          </li>
          <li>
            Share prices are flat rates. Packaged weights listed on our order
            form are <strong>estimates</strong> — every animal is different, and normal
            weight variation is not grounds for a refund or price adjustment.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-12">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-ink mb-4">2. Cancellation Policy</h2>

        <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-black/10">
          <table class="w-full text-[14px] md:text-[15px] text-left">
            <thead class="bg-pasture text-white">
              <tr>
                <th class="px-4 md:px-5 py-3 font-semibold">When you cancel</th>
                <th class="px-4 md:px-5 py-3 font-semibold">What happens to your deposit</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="text-ink/80">
              <tr class="border-t border-black/10 bg-white">
                <td class="px-4 md:px-5 py-4 align-top">
                  Within <strong>7 days (Central Time)</strong> of placing your deposit,
                  <em>and</em> before a processing (kill) date has been scheduled
                </td>
                <td class="px-4 md:px-5 py-4 align-top">
                  <strong class="text-pasture">Full refund</strong> of your deposit.
                </td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-t border-black/10 bg-cream">
                <td class="px-4 md:px-5 py-4 align-top">
                  After a processing date has been scheduled
                </td>
                <td class="px-4 md:px-5 py-4 align-top">
                  Deposit is <strong>non-refundable</strong>, but may be applied to a later
                  processing date or transferred to another customer (one time,
                  within 6 months).
                </td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-t border-black/10 bg-white">
                <td class="px-4 md:px-5 py-4 align-top">
                  After your animal has been processed
                </td>
                <td class="px-4 md:px-5 py-4 align-top">
                  The order can't be cancelled. The full balance is due, and the
                  meat is held for you per Section 4.
                </td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <ul class="mt-6 list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-[15px] text-ink/80 leading-relaxed marker:text-pasture">
          <li>
            <strong>Cut sheet changes</strong> are welcome up to <strong>7 days (Central Time) before
            your processing date</strong>. After that, the cut sheet on file is final.
          </li>
          <li>
            To cancel or make changes, email
            <a href="mailto:Coopersgrassfedbeef@gmail.com" class="text-pasture font-semibold hover:underline">Coopersgrassfedbeef@gmail.com</a>
            or call/text
            <a href="tel:2542189863" class="text-pasture font-semibold hover:underline">(254) 218-9863</a>.
            The date we receive your written request is the date used for this
            policy.
          </li>
          <li>
            If <strong>we</strong> have to cancel your order for any reason (animal health,
            processor availability, weather), you'll receive a <strong>full refund</strong> of
            everything you've paid, or you may choose to move to the next
            available animal.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-12">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-ink mb-4">3. Fulfillment &amp; Processing</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-[15px] text-ink/80 leading-relaxed marker:text-pasture">
          <li>
            Once your deposit is in, we'll confirm your share size and email you
            your <strong>processing date</strong> and an estimated ready date.
          </li>
          <li>
            Your share is cut to the preferences on your order form.
            <strong>Any cut not selected defaults to ground beef</strong> (or
            ground/sausage for pork shares).
          </li>
          <li>
            All meat is <strong>vacuum-sealed, labeled and flash-frozen</strong> before it
            leaves the processor.
          </li>
          <li>
            We'll notify you when your order is ready and send the final
            balance. Your order ships or is released for pickup once the
            balance is paid.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-12">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-ink mb-4">4. Shipping &amp; Local Pickup</h2>

        <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink mt-5 mb-3">Nationwide Shipping</h3>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-[15px] text-ink/80 leading-relaxed marker:text-pasture">
          <li>
            Orders ship frozen in insulated boxes with coolant. We ship
            <strong>Monday–Wednesday</strong> so packages are not in transit over a
            weekend; most orders arrive in <strong>1–3 business days</strong>.
          </li>
          <li>
            You'll receive tracking information when your order ships. Please
            make sure someone can bring the boxes inside and
            <strong>move the meat to a freezer right away</strong>.
          </li>
          <li>
            Please double-check your delivery address. We are not responsible
            for spoilage caused by an incorrect address, a refused delivery, or
            boxes left unattended after delivery.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink mt-6 mb-3">Local Pickup — Amarillo, TX</h3>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-[15px] text-ink/80 leading-relaxed marker:text-pasture">
          <li>Pickup is by appointment. Please bring enough cooler or freezer space for your share size.</li>
          <li>
            Orders should be picked up within <strong>7 days (Central Time)</strong> of your
            ready notice. We'll hold frozen orders for up to <strong>14 days (Central Time)</strong>;
            after that, please contact us to arrange storage or shipping.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-12">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-ink mb-4">5. Refunds &amp; Our Quality Guarantee</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-[15px] text-ink/80 leading-relaxed marker:text-pasture">
          <li>
            Because our products are perishable and custom-cut,
            <strong>we cannot accept returns</strong>.
          </li>
          <li>
            If your order arrives <strong>thawed, damaged, or with missing packages</strong>,
            contact us within <strong>24 hours of delivery (Central Time)</strong> with photos
            of the boxes and contents. We will make it right with a
            <strong>replacement, store credit, or refund</strong> for the affected items.
          </li>
          <li>
            Meat that arrives cold to the touch or partially frozen with ice
            crystals is safe and can be refrozen — this is normal for shipped
            frozen meat.
          </li>
          <li>
            Approved refunds are returned to your
            <strong>original payment method within 5–10 business days (Central Time)</strong>.
            Cash payments are refunded by Zelle or check.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-4 text-[14px] text-ink/60 italic">
          Claims made more than 24 hours after delivery, or for meat that was
          not frozen promptly after arrival, may not be eligible.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-12">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-ink mb-4">6. Questions</h2>
        <div class="bg-white border border-black/10 rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-8 text-[15px] text-ink/80 leading-relaxed">
          <p>
            We're a family operation and happy to help. Reach us at
            <a href="tel:2542189863" class="text-pasture font-semibold hover:underline">(254) 218-9863</a>
            or
            <a href="mailto:Coopersgrassfedbeef@gmail.com" class="text-pasture font-semibold hover:underline">Coopersgrassfedbeef@gmail.com</a>.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Coopers Grass Fed Beef<br />
            3201 Barry Dean Dr<br />
            Amarillo, TX
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <div class="mt-16 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a
          href="/"
          class="inline-block bg-pasture text-white font-semibold px-6 py-3 rounded-full hover:bg-pasture/90 transition"
        >
          Back to Home
        </a>
        <a
          href="/contact"
          class="inline-block bg-transparent text-pasture border border-pasture/30 font-semibold px-6 py-3 rounded-full hover:bg-pasture/5 transition"
        >
          Contact Us
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
